    "body": "Wow, very interesting; thank you for thinking this through.\n\nSo let's see. The change is:\n- Introduce a \"downgrade\" reaction. What does it do? Just set the custom element state back to \"undefined\"? That seems to work, but now I am paranoid about getting stuck in halfway states...\n- Change DOM's adoption algorithm to enqueue a downgrade reaction instead of immediately resetting the state\n\nBut we still need the change in this PR, right? This is about an entirely same-document case, with no adoption involved.\n",
