    "body": "Glad to have you here @rniwa!\n\n> I don't like the notion of \"downgrade\" because that would make the whole thing a lot more complicated.\n\nI don't think it does. It's just giving a name to the process of setting the state back to \"undefined\", which as shown by @dominiccooney's examples, is pretty necessary when adoption gets involved.\n\nIf we wanted to avoid setting the state back to undefined entirely, we could, but that would mean punting on adoption, which as @dominiccooney says, was a mistake that \"v0\" made and we should not repeat if we can avoid it.\n",
